 "title": "White Coral Bells (round)",
 "description": "The camp round, printed as \"May Bells\" in a school music book of 1916, its earliest known printing, for 2 to 4 singers: everyone sings the same tune, entering four bars apart (tenor and bass an octave lower), and its four lines sound together, one in each voice. The words are the 1916 ones.",
 "language": "en",
 "difficulty": "beginner",
